issues.problem:
§4.3 says '`f7ac37d` none on that design, 0.89 g at most on 7 others', and §17.2 says '(`f7ac37d` 7 other designs, by up to 0.89 g)'. Both sentences name their sample: every part of every 5th plausible design copied in place, from #1 and from #3, 24,221 copies. V1's f7ac37d figure covers #1 alone. I reproduced it: 14 copies on 7 pommelInBlock|C09 designs, −0.885 g at most, 73 last bits (out/cd_base_pl5a.txt).

From #3 (V1's ctrld, out/cd_base_pl5b.txt), f7ac37d moves 24 more copies on 12 designs:
- the 2 wedgeInGuard|C05 designs that round 4 also moves, with the same values;
- 6 pommelInBlock|C09 designs;
- 2 laminate|F4 designs, worst −6.908 g (laminate|F4|k0.02 wf1.5 proud-0.0200 captrue, its part 4 again in place; wf2.0 the same);
- lamHilt|hilt|w1.2 l3.0 c0.025 k0.02 proud0.000 capfalse, +5.181 g;
- a grille.
There are 73 last-bit moves on top.

Over the named sample, f7ac37d moves 38 copies on 19 designs, by up to 6.9 g. That is more than round 4's +5.6 g on #8871. For comparison, round 4 moves 11 copies on 4 designs (61 last bits) and round 5 none; both reproduced.

E-S2.14 limits its figure to 'from #1', which is true but incomplete. The plain words say 'which M3 did not do', which reads as if M3 had no such case.

